  <dt><a href="https://snipperapp.com/">SnipperApp 3</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>The AI-ready code snippet manager for macOS. Built with Swift 6 and SwiftUI, featuring MCP integration for Claude and Cursor, plus a Raycast extension.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>I set up the Snipper MCP and had Cursor import my Snibbets collection of Markdown snippets, extracting the fenced code as the snippet, applying tags from the metadata, and attaching the original Markdown file. It worked perfectly. Then I started querying Cursor about esoteric procedures and it provided me results from Snipper that were perfect. This might be my new way of handling snippets.</p>
